---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PolicyHistory from '../components/PolicyHistory.astro';
import history from '../../assets/json/vh_terms.json';
import { obfuscatedMailto, site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Privacy Policy | This is My Pattern"
  description="How thisismypattern.com handles personal information."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <article class="article prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policies</p>
      <h1>Terms and Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        thisismypattern.com is a non-profit personal website for an individual to share knowledge with the wider community. It will not get any
        commercial value from any content produced or any personal information collected.
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>1. What this website collects</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use analytics, advertising or tracking, and its own pages and scripts do not set cookies. It has no accounts, forms or
      comment system of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The website is a set of static files hosted on <a href="https://pages.github.com/">GitHub Pages</a>. When you visit, your browser sends ordinary
      requests, including your IP address, browser details and the page requested, to GitHub's servers. GitHub processes this information to deliver
      and secure the service under the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>. This
      website has no server-side code or logging of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Storage on your device</h2>
    <p>
      If you use the light/dark appearance switch, your choice is kept in your browser's session storage under the key
      <code>theme</code> so that it applies to the other pages you open. It is removed when you close the tab. See the
      <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Comments and other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Article comments are hosted on GitHub Discussions. Nothing from GitHub loads on this website's pages; following the link takes you to
      github.com, where GitHub's terms and privacy statement apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      This privacy statement does not apply to third-party websites connected by links on my website, such as LinkedIn, X and GitHub. I cannot
      guarantee that these third parties handle your personal data in a reliable or secure manner. I recommend you read the privacy statements of
      these websites prior to making use of these websites.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Email and disclosure practices</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact me by email, I use your email address and message only to reply to you. Your email address or any other personal information will
      never be shared by anyone or any party without your direct consent, unless I am required to disclose it by law or by a court order, in response
      to a law enforcement agency, or for an investigation on a matter related to public safety.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>
      I am committed to the security of personal data. I take appropriate security measures to limit abuse of and unauthorised access to personal
      data.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions or want to know which personal data I have about you, please
      <a href={obfuscatedMailto()}>contact me by email</a> or via <a href={site.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Amendments to this privacy policy</h2>
    <p>I reserve the right to make amendments to this privacy statement. Amendments can be tracked by the version history table below.</p>

    <PolicyHistory entries={history} source="/assets/json/vh_terms.json" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
